C LB-oota
"Out-of-thin-air load buffering (LB+datas). P0 reads x into r1 and stores r1 to
 y; P1 reads y into r2 and stores r2 to x. The outcome r1=r2=42 invents 42 from a
 cyclic justification. C11 PERMITS it (the thin-air problem: its relaxed-atomics
 axioms place no acyclicity on rf union dependency). Weakestmo FORBIDS it: it
 grounds reads in event structures and the cyclic OOTA configuration is never
 ew-justified / is filtered out. The Weakestmo authors state the model is
 'stronger than C11 (which allows OOTA) and weaker than RC11', so C11 is strictly
 weaker -- every separating outcome is C11-allows / Weakestmo-forbids; there is no
 reverse witness. Verdicts CITED: herd7 cannot construct an OOTA execution, so it
 reports Never. See README."
{ int x=0; int y=0; }
P0 (atomic_int* x, atomic_int* y) {
  int r1 = atomic_load_explicit(x,memory_order_relaxed);
  atomic_store_explicit(y,r1,memory_order_relaxed);
}
P1 (atomic_int* x, atomic_int* y) {
  int r2 = atomic_load_explicit(y,memory_order_relaxed);
  atomic_store_explicit(x,r2,memory_order_relaxed);
}
exists (0:r1=42 /\ 1:r2=42)
